    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0385" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg289"/>

                <head>No. 224.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Bassett.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 2,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatches numbered <pb facs="0386" n="290" xml:id="pg290"/> 143 and 146, with
                    reference to the case of Mr. Charles F. Teel, to which the latter relates. I
                    have to inform you that the Department will await a further report from you.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
